---
components: ["InterstitialScreen", "InterstitialScreenHeader", "InterstitialScreenBody", "InterstitialScreenFooter", "InterstitialScreenView"]
description: Interstitial screens walk a user through a multi-step onboarding or setup flow, hosted in a modal or as a full-screen takeover.
---

<script>
</script>

## Basic

Build an interstitial screen from `InterstitialScreenHeader`, `InterstitialScreenBody`, `InterstitialScreenFooter`, and one or more `InterstitialScreenView` steps. With a single view, the footer shows only a "Get Started" button. Bind an element to `launcherButtonRef` to return focus to it once the screen closes.

<FileSource src="/framed/InterstitialScreen/Basic" />

## Steps

Slot more than one `InterstitialScreenView` into `InterstitialScreenBody` to switch into a step-by-step, carousel-style flow.

### Multiple steps

With more than one view, `InterstitialScreenHeader` shows a `ProgressIndicator` built from each view's `stepTitle`, and `InterstitialScreenFooter` shows Skip/Back/Next, switching to "Get Started" on the final step.

<FileSource src="/framed/InterstitialScreen/MultiStep" />

## Hosting

By default, `InterstitialScreen` renders as a modal, reusing `ComposedModal`/`ModalHeader`/`ModalBody`/`ModalFooter` directly (see [Basic](#basic) above).

### Full screen

Set `isFullScreen` to render a full-screen takeover instead. `InterstitialScreenHeader`/`InterstitialScreenBody`/`InterstitialScreenFooter` render their own bare elements in this mode rather than delegating to `ModalHeader`/`ModalBody`/`ModalFooter`, and <DocKbd label="Escape" /> is handled directly since there is no modal to own it.

<FileSource src="/framed/InterstitialScreen/FullScreen" />

## Actions

`InterstitialScreenFooter` dispatches a cancelable `action` event on every Skip/Back/Next/Get-Started press, before its default behavior (navigating a step, or closing the screen) runs.

### Take over a button press

Call `event.preventDefault()` on the `action` event to block a button's default behavior, for example to require an acknowledgment before advancing.

<FileSource src="/framed/InterstitialScreen/TakeOverAction" />

### Async loading state

Bind `loadingAction` to the action name you're handling to show that button's `InlineLoading` state and disable the rest of the footer while async work runs, then advance or close the screen yourself when it resolves.

<FileSource src="/framed/InterstitialScreen/AsyncAction" />

## Closing

`InterstitialScreen` dispatches a cancelable `close` event whenever the screen is about to close: from the header close button, <DocKbd label="Escape" />, or the footer's final Skip/Get-Started action (Back/Next never close).

### Prevent default

Call `event.preventDefault()` on the `close` event to keep the screen open, for example behind a confirmation.

<FileSource src="/framed/InterstitialScreen/CancelableClose" />

### Returning focus to a launcher

Bind an element to `launcherButtonRef` to return focus to it once the screen closes, as in [Basic](#basic) above.

## Events

| Component                  | Event    | Payload                          | Cancelable |
| --------------------------- | -------- | --------------------------------- | :--------: |
| `InterstitialScreen`        | `close`  | `{ actionType }`                  |    Yes     |
| `InterstitialScreenFooter`  | `action` | `{ actionType }`                  |    Yes     |

`actionType` is one of `"close"`, `"start"`, `"skip"`, `"back"`, or `"next"` on `close`, and `"start"`, `"skip"`, `"back"`, or `"next"` on `action`.
